<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110395" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάσηλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
		ὁ</span> (cf. <i><span class="en">
			Ath.
			2.56a
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			4.139a
		</span></i>: Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>phaselos</i> is
			fem., Colum.<i><span class="en">
				10.377
			</span></i>), a kind of bean, <i>calavance, Vigna sinensis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				151
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1144
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.Com.Vet.
				5
			</span></i>, Wilcken <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				198.18
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασίολος.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> hence Lat. <i>phaselus,
				a light boat, canoe, skiff,</i> from its like ness
			to a bean-pod, Catull.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>, Hor.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Od.</u>
				3.2.29
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
